== Earlier work

My earlier work developed mathematical perspectives on neural-network function spaces and SGD dynamics. These studies helped shape my current approach to understanding large-scale learning.

- *Dynamical stability of SGD.* We studied how dynamical stability and the geometry of SGD noise shape SGD's selection among solutions that fit the data, helping explain implicit regularization in overparameterized learning. See [https://papers.nips.cc/paper/8049-how-sgd-selects-the-global-minima-in-over-parameterized-learning-a-dynamical-stability-perspective NeurIPS 2018], [https://arxiv.org/abs/2207.02628 NeurIPS 2022], [https://arxiv.org/abs/2305.17490 ICML 2023], and [https://openreview.net/forum?id=F6wmIilZXG TMLR 2026].

- *Function-space theory of neural networks.* What can neural networks approximate and learn, and how do these capabilities differ from those of kernel and random-feature methods? We studied these questions through the function spaces associated with neural networks, connecting approximation properties, architectural inductive biases, and generalization. See [https://arxiv.org/abs/1906.08039 Constructive Approximation 2021], [https://arxiv.org/abs/2108.04964 JMLR 2022], [https://arxiv.org/abs/2305.08404 NeurIPS 2023], and [https://arxiv.org/abs/2305.05642 AoS 2025].


